# CRITICAL DESIGN
# ---------------
# Geometry matching is ONLINE.
#
# At L10:
#   construct random R10 such that
#
#       cos(h10_current, R10)
#       =
#       semantic telemetry cosine at L10
#
# Apply DRA.
#
# At L11:
#   L10 has already changed the hidden state.
#
#   Therefore R11 is NOT constructed from baseline L11.
#
#   It is constructed ONLINE from the actual perturbed L11 hidden state:
#
#       cos(h11_current, R11)
#       =
#       semantic telemetry cosine at L11
#
# Thus scalar alignment, DRA envelope and brake are matched at the actual
# intervention point.
#
# IMPORTANT LIMITATION
# --------------------
# Semantic contribution magnitude also depends on ||h||.
# Geometry-matched arm inherits its own current ||h|| after L10.
# Therefore contribution equality is measured and reported, not assumed.
#
# PRIMARY ENDPOINTS
# -----------------
#   P19 = normalized physical perturbation retention L11 -> L19
#   D19 = cos(delta_h11, delta_h19)
#
# SECONDARY:
#   D27 = cos(delta_h11, delta_h27)
#
# NO fake downstream random semantic vectors are created.
# Source-energy retention is NOT used as a primary TEST114 endpoint.
#
# NULL
# ----
#   32 A-geometry-matched random controls
#   32 B-geometry-matched random controls
#
# Each replicate is averaged over the exact locked 40 prompts.
#
# DECISION
# --------
# If semantic D19 is reproduced by geometry-matched controls:
#
#   scalar local alignment is a sufficient candidate explanation.
#
# If semantic D19 remains outside matched controls:
#
#   scalar cosine/alignment is insufficient.
#
# This does NOT by itself prove "semantics" is causal.
